<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arvīds Pelše</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1899–1983</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arvīds Pelše was a Latvian communist who was first secretary of the Communist Party of Latvia from 1959 to 1966. He led the purge of the Latvian national communists in 1959 and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russification">Russification</a> and industrial growth. He later sat on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/politburo">Politburo</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> and chaired the Party Control Committee.</p></div>
